.\" Manpage for gentoo-post-install.
.TH GENTOO-POST-INSTALL 1 "2026-09-06" "gentoo-post-install 1.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gentoo\-post\-install \- post\-install automation for Gentoo Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gentoo-post-install.sh
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B sudo ./gentoo-post-install.sh
.B \-\-profile
.I desktop
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gentoo-post-install
automates post\-installation configuration for Gentoo Linux: Portage configuration
.RB ( make.conf ,
USE flags, binary package host), world maintenance, tooling, security
hardening, and an optional desktop/shell stack. It detects and drives both
.B OpenRC
and
.B systemd
and is idempotent, with a dry\-run mode and automatic backups.
.PP
Steps are numbered and can be selected individually with
.BR \-\-steps .
Most system\-changing actions are opt\-in via flags or a
.BR \-\-profile .
.SH PROFILES
.TP
.B \-\-profile \fIname\fR
One of
.BR default ", " desktop ", " server ", " hardened ", " minimal ", " opsec .
A profile sets sensible defaults that individual flags can still override.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS General
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.TP
.B \-y, \-\-yes
Assume "yes" to all prompts (non\-interactive).
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-dry\-run
Print actions without executing them.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-root
Permit running directly as root without sudo.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-banner
Do not print the ASCII banner.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-emoji
Use ASCII status markers instead of emojis.
.TP
.B \-\-log\-file \fIpath\fR
Tee a timestamped transcript to
.IR path .
.TP
.B \-\-steps \fIlist\fR
Run only these steps, e.g.
.B \-\-steps 1,2,5
or
.BR "\-\-steps 1-4" .
.TP
.B \-\-list\-steps
List all available steps and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-apps
List the known application names (for \fB\-\-apps\fR) and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-overlays
List popular overlays (for \fB\-\-overlay\fR) and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-rollback
Revert managed changes: restore
.I make.conf
from backup and remove managed drop\-in files (marked by this tool).
.SS Portage configuration
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tune
Do not modify
.IR /etc/portage/make.conf .
.TP
.B \-\-march \fInative\fR|\fInone\fR
CPU baseline (default: native).
.TP
.B \-\-jobs \fIN\fR
Force MAKEOPTS
.BR \-j N
(default: auto from cores capped by RAM).
.TP
.B \-\-accept\-license \fIdefault\fR|\fIfree\fR|\fIredist\fR|\fIall\fR
Set ACCEPT_LICENSE handling. \fIredist\fR = \fB@FREE @BINARY-REDISTRIBUTABLE\fR
(firmware), the desktop-profile default.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cpu\-flags
Do not compute CPU_FLAGS_X86 via cpuid2cpuflags.
.SS Binary packages
.TP
.B \-\-binhost
Enable the Gentoo binary package host (getbinpkg).
.TP
.B \-\-binhost\-uri \fIuri\fR
Override the binhost sync\-uri.
.SS Maintenance
.TP
.B \-\-no\-sync
Skip the Portage tree sync.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-world\-update
Skip
.BR "emerge -uUDN @world" .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-depclean
Skip
.BR "emerge --depclean" .
.TP
.B \-\-mirrors
Pick the fastest GENTOO_MIRRORS with mirrorselect before syncing.
.TP
.B \-\-merge\-config
Run \fBdispatch-conf\fR at the end to merge pending config-file updates.
.SS Kernel
.TP
.B \-\-install\-kernel
Install a distribution kernel (sys\-kernel/gentoo\-kernel\-bin).
.TP
.B \-\-kernel\-pkg \fIatom\fR
Override the kernel package atom.
.TP
.B \-\-bootloader \fIgrub\fR|\fIsystemd\-boot\fR|\fInone\fR
Bootloader wiring (sets the matching \fBinstallkernel\fR USE flag).
.TP
.B \-\-initramfs \fIdracut\fR|\fInone\fR
Initramfs generator (sets the \fBdracut\fR USE flag on installkernel).
.TP
.B \-\-kernel\-source \fIbin\fR|\fIdist\fR|\fIsource\fR|\fIvanilla\fR
Package: gentoo-kernel-bin, gentoo-kernel, gentoo-sources, vanilla-sources.
.TP
.B \-\-kernel\-config \fIstandard\fR|\fIhardened\fR|\fIminimal\fR|\fIperformance\fR
Config profile (config.d fragments; hardened = KSPP; minimal = localmodconfig).
.TP
.B \-\-kernel\-lockdown
Enable the lockdown LSM (needs signed modules or a monolithic kernel).
.TP
.B \-\-kernel\-cmdline\-harden
Add KSPP parameters to the bootloader kernel command line.
.TP
.B \-\-secure\-boot
Set up Secure Boot with app-crypt/sbctl: create keys (if absent) and sign the bootloader and kernel images. Key ENROLLMENT is left as a guided manual step (writing UEFI key stores can make the machine unbootable), and the tool prints the exact commands.
.TP
.B \-\-kernel\-manual
Leave configuration to menuconfig (no auto\-build).
.TP
.B \-\-microcode
Install CPU microcode (Intel intel\-microcode; AMD via linux\-firmware).
.SS Hardening
.TP
.B \-\-sysctl\-harden
Apply the sysctl network/kernel hardening drop\-in.
.TP
.B \-\-harden\-ipv6
Also apply IPv6 hardening knobs.
.TP
.B \-\-firewall \fInftables\fR|\fIiptables\fR|\fIufw\fR|\fInone\fR
Configure a default\-deny firewall (default backend: nftables).
.TP
.B \-\-firewall\-lan
Also allow local-network discovery (mDNS 5353, SSDP/DLNA 1900, KDE Connect 1714\-1764) on top of the default\-deny firewall. Desktop-friendly; composable with any backend.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-ssh\-rule
Do not auto\-allow SSH in the firewall (risk of lockout).
.TP
.B \-\-ssh\-harden
Write a hardened sshd_config.d drop\-in (validated with
.BR "sshd -t" ).
.TP
.B \-\-ssh\-port \fIN\fR
SSH port for the firewall allow rule and sshd.
.TP
.B \-\-ssh\-no\-root
sshd: PermitRootLogin no.
.TP
.B \-\-ssh\-key\-only
sshd: PasswordAuthentication no (a working key must exist first).
.TP
.B \-\-minimize\-surface
Blacklist risky modules, disable kexec/coredumps, tighten sysctl, mask services.
.TP
.B \-\-logs \fIoff\fR|\fIreduce\fR|\fIephemeral\fR
Minimize the log footprint (journald, shell history, dmesg).
.SS Services and monitoring
.TP
.B \-\-audit ", " \-\-no\-audit
Install (or skip) sys\-process/audit plus a system logger.
.TP
.B \-\-fail2ban ", " \-\-no\-fail2ban
Install (or skip) fail2ban with an sshd jail.
.TP
.B \-\-usbguard
Install USBGuard (opt\-in; can lock out USB input devices).
.TP
.B \-\-apparmor
Install and enable AppArmor (needs kernel LSM support).
.TP
.B \-\-hardened\-malloc
Install the hardened userspace allocator (sys\-libs/hardened_malloc, opt\-in).
.SS Shell and terminal
.TP
.B \-\-shell
Install zsh + oh\-my\-zsh + powerlevel10k + plugins.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-shell
Skip the shell setup.
.TP
.B \-\-shell\-user \fIname\fR
Configure for this user (default: the invoking sudo/current user).
.TP
.B \-\-editor \fIvim\fR|\fIneovim\fR|\fIboth\fR|\fInone\fR
Editor(s) to install (default: both).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-chsh
Do not change the user's default shell to zsh.
.SS Fonts and desktop
.TP
.B \-\-fonts
Install Nerd Fonts for the target user.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-fonts
Skip Nerd Fonts.
.TP
.B \-\-nerd\-fonts \fIlist\fR
Comma/space list of Nerd Fonts to install.
.TP
.B \-\-desktop
Install a desktop stack (Xorg, dbus/elogind, PipeWire, NetworkManager).
.TP
.B \-\-display \fIx11\fR|\fIwayland\fR|\fIboth\fR
Display server selection (default: x11).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-audio ", " \-\-no\-nm
Skip PipeWire / NetworkManager.
.TP
.B \-\-video\-cards \fIvalue\fR
Set VIDEO_CARDS manually (skip autodetection).
.SS Repositories, applications and desktop
.TP
.B \-\-overlay \fIlist\fR
Enable official overlays (guru,pentoo) via eselect\-repository, or add a
custom one as \fIname=git-url\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-apps \fIlist\fR
Install apps by name (firefox,vlc,obsidian,...) or raw atom; the app's overlay
is auto\-enabled as needed.
.TP
.B \-\-apps\-profile \fIdaily\fR|\fIdev\fR|\fImedia\fR|\fIgaming\fR
Install a ready\-made application set.
.TP
.B \-\-steam
Install native Steam (steam\-overlay, requires a multilib profile).
.TP
.B \-\-de \fIkde\fR|\fIgnome\fR|\fIsway\fR|\fIhyprland\fR|\fIxfce\fR|\fInone\fR
Install a desktop environment.
.TP
.B \-\-dm \fIsddm\fR|\fIgdm\fR|\fIlightdm\fR|\fIgreetd\fR|\fInone\fR|\fIauto\fR
Install and enable a display manager (default: per\-DE).
.SS Accounts
Passwords are read from a masked prompt and applied via
.BR chpasswd (8)
on stdin - never in argv.
.TP
.B \-\-root\-password
Set root's password.
.TP
.B \-\-disable\-root
Lock root (refused unless a non\-root wheel member exists).
.TP
.B \-\-group \fIname\fR
Create a group (repeatable).
.TP
.B \-\-user \fIspec\fR
Create/adjust a user (repeatable). \fIspec\fR is
\fBname[:sudo][:nopasswd][:groups=a,b][:shell=/bin/bash]\fR;
\fB:sudo\fR adds wheel + sudoers, \fB:nopasswd\fR grants NOPASSWD sudo (warned).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Preview the full run without making changes:
.B sudo ./gentoo-post-install.sh --dry-run
.TP
Desktop workstation, non\-interactive, with the binhost:
.B sudo ./gentoo-post-install.sh --profile desktop --binhost -y
.TP
Fresh install to a usable KDE desktop with apps:
.B sudo ./gentoo-post-install.sh --profile desktop --de kde --apps firefox,vlc,obsidian
.TP
Only tune make.conf and install tooling:
.B sudo ./gentoo-post-install.sh --steps 2,4
.TP
Revert everything this tool changed:
.B sudo ./gentoo-post-install.sh --rollback
.TP
Opsec box with an admin user and root locked:
.B sudo ./gentoo-post-install.sh --profile opsec --user 'admin:sudo' --disable-root
.TP
Hardened distribution kernel:
.B sudo ./gentoo-post-install.sh --install-kernel --kernel-source dist --kernel-config hardened
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/portage/make.conf
Tuned in place; a backup is written to
.IR /etc/portage/make.conf.gpi.bak .
.TP
.I /etc/portage/package.use/00cpu-flags, /etc/portage/package.use/10-baseline
Managed CPU flags and USE baseline.
.TP
.I /etc/sysctl.d/99-gentoo-post-install.conf
Managed sysctl hardening.
.TP
.I /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/99-gentoo-post-install.conf
Managed SSH hardening drop\-in.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
One or more steps failed, or a runtime error.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (bad option or argument).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR emerge (1),
.BR make.conf (5),
.BR portage (5),
.BR nft (8),
.BR sshd_config (5)
.SH AUTHOR
Franck FERMAN.
